From 0f5ebdbe654dfd42b3262b812bd092a54761a3d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Michael Celerier <jmcelerier@sat.qc.ca>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Directional PCF shadows: do not index the light arrays with
 split -1

findSplitIndex() returns -1 for a fragment past the last cascade split.
The hard-shadow path clamps the index before reading matrices[],
dimensionsInverted[] and atlasLocations[]; the PCF path read them at
index -1 and only masked the result afterwards with validSplit.

An out-of-bounds uniform read is undefined. On D3D12, where QRhi binds
uniform buffers as root CBVs and the shader is DXIL, it hangs the GPU:
the first opaque draw of the main pass never completes and the device is
removed (DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_HUNG, 0x887a0006). Any scene with a
DirectionalLight casting PCF shadows (the default softShadowQuality)
whose camera sees past the last split is affected; D3D11, Vulkan, OpenGL
and Metal happened to survive the read.

Clamp the index for the array reads, as the hard path does. The result
is still masked by validSplit, so the output is unchanged.
---
 .../res/effectlib/shadowMapping.glsllib              | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/runtimerender/res/effectlib/shadowMapping.glsllib b/src/runtimerender/res/effectlib/shadowMapping.glsllib
index 5471e55a..79d205fe 100644
--- a/src/runtimerender/res/effectlib/shadowMapping.glsllib
+++ b/src/runtimerender/res/effectlib/shadowMapping.glsllib
@@ -235,10 +235,14 @@ ShadowResult qt_sampleDirectionalLight_pcf(in int lightIndex, in float zDepthVie
     // Using a mask instead of early return
     float validSplit = step(0.0, float(splitIndex)); // 1.0 if splitIndex >= 0, 0.0 otherwise
 
-    // Get current split shadow data
-    vec4 projCoord = ubDirectionalLights.directionalLights[lightIndex].matrices[splitIndex] * vec4(worldPos, 1.0);
-    vec3 dimensions = ubDirectionalLights.directionalLights[lightIndex].dimensionsInverted[splitIndex].xyz;
-    vec4 shadowAtlasInfo = ubDirectionalLights.directionalLights[lightIndex].atlasLocations[splitIndex];
+    // Get current split shadow data. splitIndex is -1 past the last split;
+    // the result is then masked by validSplit, but the arrays must not be
+    // indexed with it: out-of-bounds uniform reads are undefined, and on
+    // D3D12 (root CBV, DXIL) they hang the GPU.
+    int safeSplitIndex = max(splitIndex, 0);
+    vec4 projCoord = ubDirectionalLights.directionalLights[lightIndex].matrices[safeSplitIndex] * vec4(worldPos, 1.0);
+    vec3 dimensions = ubDirectionalLights.directionalLights[lightIndex].dimensionsInverted[safeSplitIndex].xyz;
+    vec4 shadowAtlasInfo = ubDirectionalLights.directionalLights[lightIndex].atlasLocations[safeSplitIndex];
     float layerIndex = shadowAtlasInfo.w;
     vec2 uvAtlasOffset = shadowAtlasInfo.xy;
     float uvAtlasScale = shadowAtlasInfo.z;
-- 
2.43.0

